---
description: Forms (React Hook Form + validation) and navigation conventions
globs: ["**/*Form*.tsx", "**/forms/**/*.tsx", "src/app/**/*.tsx", "**/navigation/**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Forms

- Use React Hook Form (`react-hook-form`) for any form with > 1 field.
- Build reusable form components (`FormField`, `FormSubmit`) on top of the UI
  primitives — never re-implement label / error layout per screen.
- Centralize validation schemas (Zod) in `src/features/<name>/schemas/`.
  Same schema validates the form AND the API response.
- Never duplicate validation logic between client and server boundaries.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — validation re-stated in two places
if (phone.length !== 10) showError('…');
const parsed = z.string().length(10).parse(phone);

// ✅ GOOD — one schema, both sides
const phoneSchema = z.string().length(10);
const result = phoneSchema.safeParse(phone);
```

# Navigation

- Use Expo Router. Routes live ONLY in `src/app/`.
- Centralize route names as constants (`src/constants/routes.ts`) — no
  string-literal `router.push('/auth/otp')` calls in screens.
- Type navigation params at the route level (Expo Router's typed routes feature).
- Keep navigation config (initial route, deep-link prefixes, screen options)
  centralized in `src/app/_layout.tsx`.
- Deep links MUST validate their payload before applying (e.g., OTP autofill).
